WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.160
You are parking a car in a narrow garage.

00:00:02.960 --> 00:00:05.240
The car is narrower than the door, so it
fits.

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:08.920
But park too far to one side, and you
still scrape the wall.

00:00:09.480 --> 00:00:13.440
Process capability works the same way, and
it takes two numbers to see it.

00:00:14.280 --> 00:00:16.380
A bakery makes cookies for the campus
café.

00:00:17.100 --> 00:00:20.220
Every cookie should weigh between 94 and
106 grams.

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:23.620
Those are the lower and upper
specification limits.

00:00:24.380 --> 00:00:29.560
The standard deviation is 1.5 grams, and
right now the average cookie weighs 103

00:00:29.560 --> 00:00:30.120
grams.

00:00:30.820 --> 00:00:31.920
Is this process capable?

00:00:32.520 --> 00:00:33.500
Pause and decide.

00:00:34.520 --> 00:00:38.320
Start with Cp. It compares the width of
the specs to the width of the process.

00:00:39.080 --> 00:00:40.800
The specs are 12 grams wide.

00:00:41.500 --> 00:00:43.680
The process spread is 6 standard
deviations,

00:00:44.500 --> 00:00:45.360
which is 9 grams.

00:00:46.220 --> 00:00:48.620
12 divided by 9 is 1.33.

00:00:49.420 --> 00:00:50.960
That meets the usual target.

00:00:51.580 --> 00:00:53.100
The car is narrower than the garage.

00:00:53.100 --> 00:00:56.800
But Cp never asks where the process is
centred.

00:00:57.540 --> 00:00:58.540
The average is 103,

00:00:59.440 --> 00:01:03.100
not 100, so the heavy tail spills past the
upper limit.

00:01:03.920 --> 00:01:05.380
Cpk checks the centre.

00:01:05.840 --> 00:01:09.620
Measure from the average to each limit,
then divide by three standard deviations,

00:01:10.280 --> 00:01:11.540
which is 4.5 grams.

00:01:12.320 --> 00:01:15.180
On the upper side, 106 minus 103 is 3.

00:01:15.820 --> 00:01:18.640
3 divided by 4.5 is 0.67.

00:01:18.640 --> 00:01:21.260
On the lower side, the distance is 9.

00:01:21.780 --> 00:01:24.040
9 divided by 4.5 is 2.

00:01:24.540 --> 00:01:26.280
Cpk is the smaller result.

00:01:27.100 --> 00:01:28.020
0.67.

00:01:28.820 --> 00:01:30.020
The process is not capable.

00:01:31.060 --> 00:01:33.280
The gap between the two numbers tells you
what to fix.

00:01:34.180 --> 00:01:35.380
Cp says the spread is fine.

00:01:36.220 --> 00:01:39.380
Cpk says the centre is off, so leave the
oven alone.

00:01:40.240 --> 00:01:45.860
Move the average back to 100 grams, and
Cpk rises to 1.33, the

00:01:45.860 --> 00:01:46.480
same as Cp.

00:01:47.440 --> 00:01:48.960
Cp asks, could it fit?

00:01:49.560 --> 00:01:51.320
Cpk asks, does it fit right now?
